WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.610 --> 00:00:01.830
Let's talk about Iowa.

00:00:01.830 --> 00:00:05.670
We still, as of this recording, don't have
final results from the Iowa caucus, the first

00:00:05.670 --> 00:00:08.420
in the nation primary, which took place on
Monday night.

00:00:08.420 --> 00:00:12.870
It is time now to just very clearly say with
no ifs, ands and buts.

00:00:12.870 --> 00:00:15.469
No caveats, no restrictions whatsoever.

00:00:15.469 --> 00:00:19.380
Iowa can't get the privilege of being the
first to vote in primary elections anymore,

00:00:19.380 --> 00:00:20.380
period.

00:00:20.380 --> 00:00:21.380
Full stop.

00:00:21.380 --> 00:00:25.350
Now, there are a whole bunch of reasons for
this and most of the reasons why Iowa actually

00:00:25.350 --> 00:00:29.630
shouldn't be the first to vote, have nothing
to do with the fiasco from Monday night.

00:00:29.630 --> 00:00:34.220
The benefit of the fiasco from Monday night,
if there is one, if there is a silver lining,

00:00:34.220 --> 00:00:39.970
is that it's a good opportunity to put back
in the spotlight that Iowa should not get

00:00:39.970 --> 00:00:41.970
the privilege of being first to vote.

00:00:41.970 --> 00:00:45.460
It's nothing personal against Iowa or Iowa.

00:00:45.460 --> 00:00:49.710
Iowans are perfectly nice people, uh, the,
the ones that I've met, but this is a much

00:00:49.710 --> 00:00:51.840
bigger problem that we are dealing with here.

00:00:51.840 --> 00:00:57.560
First and foremost, Iowa is not remotely representative
of the democratic electorate nor of the country's

00:00:57.560 --> 00:00:59.280
demographics in any way.

00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:01.840
There's just no factual reason.

00:01:01.840 --> 00:01:06.700
There's no empirical case for Iowa getting
to be the first to vote when it comes to race

00:01:06.700 --> 00:01:07.700
and ethnicity.

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:08.720
It's very obvious.

00:01:08.720 --> 00:01:12.430
Iowa and New Hampshire, the first two to vote
are 90% white.

00:01:12.430 --> 00:01:16.250
The country is 60% white when it comes to
economics.

00:01:16.250 --> 00:01:22.450
When it comes to education, there is no mathematical
or empirical justification for Iowa being

00:01:22.450 --> 00:01:29.020
the place where it makes sense to start and
going first does carry disproportionate influence

00:01:29.020 --> 00:01:31.229
over the eventual subsequent primaries.

00:01:31.229 --> 00:01:36.590
There's a good Vox piece from a couple of
days ago which reminds us that there was a

00:01:36.590 --> 00:01:44.010
37 point swing in the national polls when
John Kerry won in Iowa and New Hampshire 16

00:01:44.010 --> 00:01:47.400
years ago in the 2004 democratic primary.

00:01:47.400 --> 00:01:52.850
Now then we get to the disaster on Monday
night, the fiasco Monday night with the app

00:01:52.850 --> 00:01:57.229
crashing and the results being delayed and
immediate foul play and conspiracy theories

00:01:57.229 --> 00:01:58.329
exploding.

00:01:58.329 --> 00:02:03.910
It doesn't help Iowa's case and it is another
reason for realistically not even having a

00:02:03.910 --> 00:02:08.830
single state be the first to vote, but instead
having a number of States being the first

00:02:08.830 --> 00:02:09.830
to vote.

00:02:09.830 --> 00:02:11.270
You could organize this any number of different
ways.

00:02:11.270 --> 00:02:13.959
You could say, well, we will divide the country
into regions.

00:02:13.959 --> 00:02:18.220
We'll have the Northeast and the Southeast
and we'll have the West coast, whatever, and

00:02:18.220 --> 00:02:23.790
we will have one state from each region vote
first on the first primary day.

00:02:23.790 --> 00:02:28.750
Or we could say if we really are convinced
that we want to have one state go first and

00:02:28.750 --> 00:02:33.800
one state only, which I don't think makes
sense, you could at least rotate the state

00:02:33.800 --> 00:02:37.700
or you could pick a different state that is
more Def demographically representative of

00:02:37.700 --> 00:02:38.700
the country.

00:02:38.700 --> 00:02:43.560
Like for example, Illinois is often mentioned
because of its racial and ethnic and educational

00:02:43.560 --> 00:02:48.330
breakdown, uh, as compared to the country
at large, it would be a much better fit.

00:02:48.330 --> 00:02:52.120
You could use similar metrics, other good
options for which States should go first.

00:02:52.120 --> 00:02:56.810
If we're trying to have a state that's representative
of the country, you can look at New Jersey,

00:02:56.810 --> 00:02:58.480
you could look at New York, you could look
at Florida.

00:02:58.480 --> 00:02:59.770
It doesn't have to be a blue state.

00:02:59.770 --> 00:03:03.910
Remember, it's the democratic primary that
we're talking about and this is also a good

00:03:03.910 --> 00:03:09.959
time to mention that there is nothing in the
constitution about how primaries are supposed

00:03:09.959 --> 00:03:10.989
to be run.

00:03:10.989 --> 00:03:15.450
A lot of people don't realize that the democratic
and the Republican parties, these are not

00:03:15.450 --> 00:03:21.470
government entities and primaries are not
real elections in a sense.

00:03:21.470 --> 00:03:23.250
In a sense they are, but in a sense they are
not.

00:03:23.250 --> 00:03:27.720
And what I mean by that is that the process
and the rules and the parameters for these

00:03:27.720 --> 00:03:33.190
primaries are decided on by the parties and
the members of the parties.

00:03:33.190 --> 00:03:35.510
And of course at the state level.

00:03:35.510 --> 00:03:37.330
And we're going to get to that cause that
is a factor.

00:03:37.330 --> 00:03:43.410
Back in 2016 you could tell a lot of people
didn't realize that parties decide how to

00:03:43.410 --> 00:03:48.450
run the primaries because people were looking
at what the DNC did in terms of how they structured

00:03:48.450 --> 00:03:54.000
the debates and how they helped Hillary Clinton
as maybe being illegal was not illegal.

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:55.110
This was not a legal issue.

00:03:55.110 --> 00:03:57.520
What the DNC did in 2016.

00:03:57.520 --> 00:04:02.260
Now you do have state law and state constitutions
that make this more complicated.

00:04:02.260 --> 00:04:07.860
You have a, for example, uh, lots of States
have laws about when the primary is supposed

00:04:07.860 --> 00:04:08.940
to happen.

00:04:08.940 --> 00:04:15.020
Iowa says that it's caucus must happen eight
days before any other state's proceedings.

00:04:15.020 --> 00:04:19.139
That's why New Hampshire is eight days after
Iowa's caucus.

00:04:19.139 --> 00:04:24.639
New Hampshire has a law that says they must
be the first primary, which is why Iowa goes

00:04:24.639 --> 00:04:30.059
first, but it's a caucus and not a primary,
so I don't want to pretend that getting States

00:04:30.059 --> 00:04:33.139
to change their laws about this is easy.

00:04:33.139 --> 00:04:37.490
It's difficult for sure, but the DNC can push
them if they want to.

00:04:37.490 --> 00:04:42.030
It's not clear that the DNC wants to change
the system that we have so much like the electoral

00:04:42.030 --> 00:04:43.030
college.

00:04:43.030 --> 00:04:46.919
More broadly, we are dealing with what are
effectively outdated and broken systems at

00:04:46.919 --> 00:04:47.919
this point.

00:04:47.919 --> 00:04:54.039
Even the delegate system needs to be, you
could do a national vote in the entire country

00:04:54.039 --> 00:04:58.610
on the same day with instant runoff voting
at the state level, giving everybody more

00:04:58.610 --> 00:05:02.810
equal say and equal influence regardless of
where it is that they live.

00:05:02.810 --> 00:05:08.740
My preference would be to come up with a way
to have more States go first, if not all,

00:05:08.740 --> 00:05:11.840
or to rotate who gets to go first?

00:05:11.840 --> 00:05:17.580
Why would it be bad for Connecticut Democrats
or Washington state Democrats to go first

00:05:17.580 --> 00:05:18.719
every once in a while?

00:05:18.719 --> 00:05:25.919
It wouldn't be unless you want to perpetuate
the DNCs stranglehold, an influence over the

00:05:25.919 --> 00:05:27.529
way that this is run.

00:05:27.529 --> 00:05:33.160
That being said, this will not solve if you
have a different state, go first.

00:05:33.160 --> 00:05:38.699
That state still has disproportionate power
and influence and makes a bigger impact and

00:05:38.699 --> 00:05:44.780
that is ultimately something that the DNC
wants because it makes the primary easier

00:05:44.780 --> 00:05:45.899
to control.

00:05:45.899 --> 00:05:51.919
Uh, also just as a, as a Coda, the first primary
shouldn't be a caucus and in fact, I would

00:05:51.919 --> 00:05:53.969
support getting rid of caucuses altogether,
period.

00:05:53.969 --> 00:06:00.409
And any process that involves coin flips and
requires hours of participation is outdated.

00:06:00.409 --> 00:06:07.159
I won't call it bad, it's just not realistically
fine tuned and a good process in 2020 change

00:06:07.159 --> 00:06:08.159
my mind.

00:06:08.159 --> 00:06:09.159
I want to hear from you.

00:06:09.159 --> 00:06:11.020
I'm on Twitter at the Pacman.

00:06:11.020 --> 00:06:12.069
Follow me there.

00:06:12.069 --> 00:06:12.993
We'll take a quick break and be back right
after this

